> component breakdown needs Claude Code ≥ 2.1.259 — 2 sessions are older or lack a tool snapshot

## Baseline

B is the context of a session's first call (input + cache read + cache creation): exact. Every call re-reads it, so its token-turns share is B × N / Σ context over the session's N calls.

**Pooled share (headline): 97.6%** of all input read by the 2 eligible main sessions is the fixed baseline. Typical session: 97.6% (median of per-session shares, median N = 3; this mostly reflects session length).

| Sessions | n | B p50 | B p90 | Pooled share | Typical session | Median N |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| main | 2 | 4,000 | — | 97.6% | 97.6% | 3 |
| subagent (fixed overhead + task prompt) | 0 | — | — | — | — | — |

B p90 is printed only from 10 sessions.

